      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "VRChat should also encourage Canny feedback in other languages too. While Canny being supported in different languages is a different game, and not VRChat's fault, it would still be beneficial to the platform to hear from all voices. The amount of feedback given in a foreign language is quite minimal. I'd like to see more users contribute.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    }
  ],
  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2022-08-02T06:33:55.595Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "The current tutorial world has too few features, teaches only the bare minimum of functionality, and\nIt is thrown in like bait where there are unpleasant users from different cultures.\nAlso, VRC has added too many features.\nThe official tutorial world should allow users to choose the language of the explanations, so that users who are not native English speakers can understand them better.\nAlso, put some public world portal links for each language so that people can be intuitively directed to where people in each language congregate.\n(An officially selected world would be great.)\nAlso, until the VISITOR becomes a USER, you can create a column dedicated to tutorials and put the official tutorial worlds and\nIt would be good to create a column dedicated to tutorials until the VISITOR becomes a USER, so that the tutorial can be viewed at any time in the official tutorial world or the equivalent world for each language.\nIn Japan, a unique community has been formed in the tutorial world.\nIf such communities in each country make it easier for unfamiliar users to find the worlds, it will be easier to guide them.\n(To be honest, it is not too late to start the cross-language exchange after you are somewhat familiar with VRC.)\nPlease let us know if there is anything we should add to Tutorial.\nTranslated with www.DeepL.com/Translator (free version)",
